[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: dates parse month first in EU locales. Its
reports hold two problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

<Callout kind="warn">
One fix for the parser will not close this. The hint reports come from a form bug in booking-v3,
not from the parser.
</Callout>

## The two problems

**parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants all write the day first,
so 7 June arrives as 6 July. Every report from the app or email, and every form report from a
booking-v2 tenant, is this.
A swap can only happen when the day is 12 or less, so most dates still parse right.

**hint.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint says, month
first, and the form reads it the tenant's way, day first. The swap looks the same as the parser's,
but the fix is in the form, not the parser. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants
(alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) are this.

**Read as a one-day move.** The desk read five parser reports as a date one day early, not swapped
(`desk-notes.json`, `oneDayMove`). By tenant and channel they are parser reports, so they are
counted there and footnoted under the table.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match.
Both problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so
subject matching put them in one ticket. Intake's tag does not help either: it is a guess from the
browser and disagrees with the tenant's cause for 38 reports. Tell the problems apart by tenant,
form and channel (`causes.ts`).

## How the counts were made

- Source: `reports-4471.json` from the ticket system. It has 427 rows; 15 are the same report twice
  from overlapping export pages. One id is one report.
- Cause by tenant locale, booking form and channel (`causes.ts`), not by intake tag.
- Reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) stay with their cause and are footnoted.
  Of the 412 bodies, 403 describe a day/month swap, 5 are those one-day reads, and 4 name no dates.

